# Deploy Live (Windows Server)

Standing instruction (Urdu): **"ab jo bhe change krna direct deployed krty jana"** — after any runtime-affecting change, deploy immediately. Never leave server-side fixes local-only.

## Target

| | |
|---|---|
| **Server** | `5.226.139.8` (Windows) |
| **Path** | `C:\burjex` |
| **Retired** | `187.127.215.195` — **never deploy** unless user explicitly asks |

Config: `deploy/windows-server/DEPLOY_TARGET.env`

## Deploy workflow

1. **Push code:** WinRM / hotpatch only the affected trees to `C:\burjex` (CRM, gateway, market-data, bridge as relevant).
2. **Restart stack:** Use `deploy/windows-server/` helpers — they always pass `--env-file deploy/.env.prod.ip`:
   - `.\up.ps1` — build + start
   - `.\recreate.ps1 <service>` — force recreate one service
   - `.\restart.ps1 <service>` — restart
   - **Never** run raw `docker compose up/restart/recreate` without `--env-file` (causes market-data crash-loop).
3. **Bridge:** After `mt5_bridge` changes, restart NSSM service `BurjexMt5Bridge` on the server.

## What to redeploy

| Changed | Redeploy |
|---|---|
| Django CRM | `.\recreate.ps1 crm-web` or `.\up.ps1 --build` |
| BTrader gateway / ws / engine | matching `btrader-*` service via `.\recreate.ps1` |
| market-data / feed | `.\recreate.ps1 btrader-market-data` |
| MT5 bridge | hotpatch + restart bridge service |

## Flutter / mobile

When Flutter or mobile app code changes: rebuild release APK and copy to user Desktop as `BurjexPrime-LIVE.apk`.

## Agent permissions

Use `required_permissions: ["all"]` for deploy, WinRM, and shell commands — do not ask the user repeatedly to Allow.